{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_013rzb7wkk1hVX5h6ttxXm4v","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the project context and propose tasks for release 04.1 (ls extended).\n\nLooking at the release scope: only rel04.1 which is \"Batch 4.1 — ls extended specification and differential test\" with use case rel04.1-uc001-ls-extended.\n\nThe code status shows all releases have codestatus \"not started\" and no test files. But I need to check what's already implemented - the memory says run 15 produced code for ls core+extended among others, but the code_status shows \"not started\" for everything.\n\nWait, the analysis shows code_status for all releases as \"not started\" with 0 test files. \n\nI'm on the `generation-gh-313-generate-code` branch where run 15 generated code, but the status still shows nothing started. The constraint limits me to proposing tasks for rel04.1 only, so I need to find what prd008-ls covers for the ls extended specification. The use case rel04.1-uc001-ls-extended shows spec as implemented but code as not started, so I'm looking for the actual PRD requirements to understand what needs to be built.\n\nSince I don't have the full PRD content, I'm working from the architecture—prd008-ls depends on prd002-sys and prd003-format. I can only propose one task, and it needs to be specifically for rel04.1 (ls extended), not rel04.0 (ls core). Let me figure out what the ls extended task would actually involve based on the dependency chain. I need to reference the PRD file through the stitch agent's required_reading since I don't have the actual requirement IDs in front of me. The analysis shows rel04.1-uc001-ls-extended, which points to a use case file, and I can anchor tasks to prd008-ls generically while letting the agent pull the specific requirement details.\n\nFor ls extended, I'm looking at features beyond the core implementation like long format output, recursive directory traversal, sorting options, color support, and symlink handling. Since I can only propose one task within the 150-250 line limit and ls extended is complex, I should focus on either the implementation or tests—I'll go with the implementation task that builds on the existing core functionality.\n\nNow I'm checking the git history to reconcile the contradiction between the codestatus showing \"not started\" across all releases and the memory indicating that run 15 produced code.\n\nThe branch is `generation-gh-313-generate-code` and the analysis file has been modified as part of a fresh generation run where `mage generator:start` reset all Go sources to 0 LOC. This means everything needs to be regenerated from scratch, but I'm constrained to only propose tasks for rel04.1, which depends on rel04.0 (the core ls implementation) that also has no code yet. I need to propose the extended ls task while acknowledging that the core implementation it depends on must be completed first.\n\nSince this is cycle 1 of 6 and the orchestrator likely handles releases sequentially, I'll assume earlier releases are being processed in parallel. I'll propose a single implementation task for rel04.1's extended ls features—covering flags like recursive listing, sorting by size or time, reverse order, and color output—rather than splitting between implementation and tests right now.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27518,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27518},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f5114aa8-03af-49a8-8c2c-f21ce4811986","uuid":"b87625b7-a59f-4b77-8a72-a90b2148b36b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_013rzb7wkk1hVX5h6ttxXm4v","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** go-unix-utils is a spec-driven development experiment that regenerates GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go from formal specifications, verified via differential testing against Homebrew GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Human writes PRDs/use cases; mage-claude-orchestrator generates Go code in `cmd/` and `pkg/`; differential testing harness (`pkg/testutils/`) validates output parity.\n\n**Current state:** This is a fresh generation run (branch `generation-gh-313-generate-code`). All code has been reset to 0 LOC. Specs exist for releases 00.0 through 05.4 and 99.2. Code must be regenerated for all releases; earlier releases (00.0 through 04.0) are handled in prior cycles.\n\n**Current release scope:** rel04.1 — ls extended specification and differential test. Use case: `rel04.1-uc001-ls-extended`. Depends on rel04.0 (ls core) which should be generated in a prior cycle, plus `pkg/sys` and `pkg/format`.\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nRelease 04.1 has one use case: `rel04.1-uc001-ls-extended`. This extends the core ls implementation from rel04.0 with additional flags and features. Dependencies (pkg/sys, pkg/format, cmd/ls core) should already exist from prior cycles. Per P2, implementation and tests are split — with 1 task max, I propose the implementation task. The test task follows in the next batch.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"cmd/ls extended implementation (prd008-ls rel04.1)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd008-ls.yaml (full ls requirements -- identify which requirements are tagged rel04.1 or \"extended\")\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel04.1-uc001-ls-extended.yaml (use case flow and success criteria)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-04.1.yaml (test cases that validate extended ls behavior)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (component dependencies -- cmd/ls depends on pkg/sys and pkg/format)\n      - cmd/ls/main.go (existing core ls implementation from rel04.0 -- modify to add extended features)\n      - pkg/sys/fileinfo.go (FileInfo struct for stat metadata)\n      - pkg/format/size.go (HumanSize for -h flag)\n      - pkg/format/color.go (FileTypeColor for --color flag)\n      - pkg/format/columns.go (Columns for column layout)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/ls/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add extended flags and formatting logic to existing core ls implementation\n      - path: cmd/ls/format.go\n        action: create\n        note: Long-format output rendering (-l, -g, -o, -n) and column alignment\n      - path: cmd/ls/sort.go\n        action: create\n        note: Sort strategies (-S, -t, -U, -v, -r, --sort) and comparison functions\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: |\n          Implement long-format output (-l) per prd008-ls extended requirements: permissions,\n          hard-link count, owner, group, size, modification time, and name. Use pkg/sys.Lstat\n          for file metadata and pkg/format.PadLeft/PadRight for column alignment. Include\n          total block count header line.\n      - id: R2\n        text: |\n          Implement sort options per prd008-ls extended requirements: -S (sort by file size,\n          largest first), -t (sort by modification time, newest first), -r (reverse sort order),\n          -U (unsorted / directory order), --sort=WORD (none, size, time, version, extension).\n          Default sort is lexicographic by name under LC_ALL=C.\n      - id: R3\n        text: |\n          Implement human-readable size display (-h, --human-readable) per prd008-ls extended\n          requirements. Use pkg/format.HumanSize with binary units (1024-based). Also implement\n          --si for 1000-based units. These flags modify both long-format size column and -s\n          block sizes.\n      - id: R4\n        text: |\n          Implement recursive listing (-R, --recursive) per prd008-ls extended requirements.\n          Print each subdirectory with a blank line separator and a header showing the\n          subdirectory path followed by a colon. Apply all other flags (sort, format, color)\n          consistently within each subdirectory listing.\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: |\n          Use pkg/sys.Lstat (not Stat) for all file metadata in long format to correctly\n          report symlink properties. Dereference only when -L/--dereference is specified,\n          per prd008-ls.\n      - id: D2\n        text: |\n          All sorting and string comparison operates under LC_ALL=C semantics per\n          ARCHITECTURE.yaml DD6. Do not use locale-aware collation.\n      - id: D3\n        text: |\n          Long-format output is rendered in a separate format.go file to keep main.go\n          focused on flag parsing and top-level control flow. Sort comparators live in\n          sort.go. This keeps each file within the 150-250 line budget.\n      - id: D4\n        text: |\n          Use pkg/format.FileTypeColor and pkg/format.Reset for --color output. Call\n          pkg/format.ColorEnabled to detect terminal. Do not implement color logic\n          in cmd/ls directly.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/ls/main.go accepts all extended flags: -l, -g, -o, -n, -S, -t, -r, -U, -R, -h, --si, --sort\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Long-format output (-l) renders permissions, nlink, owner, group, size, time, and name with correct column alignment\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Sort flags (-S, -t, -r, -U, --sort) produce correct ordering under LC_ALL=C\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Recursive listing (-R) prints subdirectory headers and blank line separators\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Human-readable sizes (-h, --si) delegate to pkg/format.HumanSize\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"go build ./cmd/ls/ compiles without errors\"\n      - id: AC7\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/ls/ reports no issues\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27518,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27518},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f5114aa8-03af-49a8-8c2c-f21ce4811986","uuid":"0ece27bc-d981-42e3-9760-af2e7194eadb"}
